.TH QEMATE 1 "July 17, 2026" "Qemate 4.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
qemate \- Hardened QEMU virtual machine manager for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qemate
.I COMMAND
[
.I NAME
] [
.I OPTIONS
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Qemate
is a streamlined command-line utility for managing QEMU virtual machines (VMs). It simplifies VM creation, control, and configuration, leveraging QEMU with KVM acceleration for enhanced performance when supported by the host system.

QEMU 10.0 or newer is required. Commands that create or resize images or launch a VM reject older QEMU tool versions.

All commands are top-level with hyphenated names. There are no subcommand groups.

.SH COMMANDS
.SS VM Management
.TP
.B create NAME [OPTIONS]
Create a new VM with optimized defaults for Linux or Windows.
.RS
.TP
.B --os-type TYPE
OS preset (\fBlinux\fR|\fBwindows\fR; default: linux).
.TP
.B --memory SIZE
Memory size (e.g., \fB4G\fR, \fB2048M\fR).
.TP
.B --cores N
Number of CPU cores (1\(en64).
.TP
.B --disk-size SIZE
Virtual disk size (e.g., \fB60G\fR). Creates a qcow2 image. Mutually exclusive with \fB--disk-dev\fR.
.TP
.B --disk-dev PATH
Raw physical block device to use instead of a qcow2 image (e.g., \fB/dev/sdb\fR). \fB--disk-size\fR is ignored when this is set. Resize is not supported on physical-device VMs.
.TP
.B --machine TYPE[,accel=kvm|tcg]
Machine type (e.g., \fBq35,accel=kvm\fR).
.TP
.B --enable-audio / --no-audio
Enable or disable PCIe audio passthrough. Requires \fBAUDIO_PASSTHROUGH_PCI\fR to be set in the VM config after creation.
.TP
.B --enable-tpm / --no-tpm
Enable TPM 2.0 emulation (requires \fBswtpm\fR and \fBswtpm_setup\fR).
.TP
.B --uefi / --no-uefi
Enable or disable UEFI firmware (default: on for Windows, off for Linux). Requires \fBedk2-ovmf\fR.
.TP
.B --spice / --no-spice
Enable SPICE display server (default port: 5930).
.TP
.B --share-backend auto|virtfs|smb|virtiofs
Select the shared folder backend.
.TP
.B --profile balanced|performance
Select the portable balanced policy (default) or opt in to preallocated, locked memory and tuned VirtIO queues. New performance-profile Windows VMs use VirtIO block and require its storage driver during installation.
.RE

.TP
.B start NAME [OPTIONS]
Start a VM.
.RS
.TP
.B --headless
Start without a graphical console.
.TP
.B --iso PATH
Attach a primary ISO image for installation.
.TP
.B --virtio-iso PATH
Attach a secondary ISO (e.g., VirtIO-Win drivers for Windows guests).
.TP
.B --debug
Print the full generated QEMU command to stderr before launching.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Print the shell-escaped effective QEMU command without binding host devices, creating TAP interfaces, or starting helper daemons.
.RE

.TP
.B stop NAME [--timeout SECONDS] [--force]
Request an orderly guest ACPI shutdown through QMP and wait up to 60 seconds by default. If the guest does not stop, it is left running. \fB--force\fR sends SIGKILL immediately.

.TP
.B delete NAME [--force]
Delete a VM and all its data. Prompts for confirmation unless \fB--force\fR is used. Locked VMs require \fB--force\fR.

.TP
.B resize NAME SIZE|+SIZE [--force]
Resize the VM disk image (e.g., \fB80G\fR or \fB+20G\fR). The VM must be stopped. \fB--force\fR is accepted for CLI compatibility but does not allow live qcow2 resizing. Not supported for physical-device VMs (\fB--disk-dev\fR).

.TP
.B list
List all VMs with seven columns: NAME, STATUS, LOCKED, OS, AUDIO, TPM, SPICE.

.TP
.B status NAME
Display detailed VM configuration and runtime status, including CPU, memory, disk, network, UEFI state, share backend, port forwards, USB passthrough, and shared folders.

.TP
.B configure NAME
.TQ
.B config NAME
Open the VM config file directly in \fB$EDITOR\fR (falls back to \fBnano\fR). After editing, the config is validated against the Qemate schema; if validation fails, the previous config is automatically restored. The VM must be stopped before configuring.

.TP
.B tune NAME balanced|performance
Change the VM runtime performance policy without replacing custom disk, network, passthrough, or shared-folder settings. The VM must be stopped.

.TP
.B doctor [NAME]
Report host KVM, QMP client, AVIC, vhost-net, and memlock readiness. With a VM name, also show effective storage, memory, and shared-folder choices.

.SS Port Forwarding
.TP
.B port-add NAME [IP:]HOST:GUEST[:tcp|udp]
Add a port forwarding rule. Protocol defaults to \fBtcp\fR if omitted.

.TP
.B port-remove NAME [IP:]HOST:GUEST[:tcp|udp]
Remove a port forwarding rule.

.SS USB Passthrough
.TP
.B usb-add NAME VENDOR:PRODUCT
Attach a host USB device by vendor:product ID (see \fBlsusb\fR(8)).

.TP
.B usb-remove NAME VENDOR:PRODUCT
Detach a host USB device.

.TP
.B usb-list NAME
List all USB devices configured for the VM.

.SS Shared Folders
.TP
.B share-add NAME [TAG:]PATH
Add a shared directory. The tag is auto-derived from the folder name if omitted.

.TP
.B share-remove NAME TAG
Remove a shared directory by its tag.

.TP
.B share-list NAME
List all configured shared folders for the VM.

.SS VM Protection
.TP
.B lock NAME
Lock a VM to prevent modification or deletion.

.TP
.B unlock NAME
Unlock a VM.

.SH NETWORK BACKENDS
.TP
.B user
SLiRP userspace NAT. Default; no host setup required.
.TP
.B passt
Unprivileged backend using the host network stack directly (requires \fBpasst\fR).
.TP
.B tap
Kernel-accelerated TAP interface with optional host bridge. Requires \fBiproute2\fR and a pre-configured host bridge. Fastest option.
.TP
.B none
No network interface attached to the VM.

.SH SHARED FOLDER BACKENDS
.TP
.B auto
Picks the best available backend: virtiofs \(-> virtfs for Linux guests, smb for Windows guests.
.TP
.B virtfs
9P filesystem. Linux guests only; no extra host dependencies.
.TP
.B virtiofs
High-performance VirtIO-FS. Supports multiple simultaneous shared folders. Requires \fBvirtiofsd\fR. Windows guests also need WinFSP and the VirtIO-FS driver.
.TP
.B smb
QEMU user-mode SMB share. Windows guests only; limited to one folder. Requires \fBsmbd\fR from Samba on the host and NETWORK_TYPE=user or nat.

.SH SECURITY & CONCURRENCY
Qemate implements strict \fBflock\fR-based locking on configuration files to prevent race conditions during simultaneous CLI commands. The script operates with a \fBumask 0077\fR to ensure all created files are accessible only by the owner. Config files are loaded via a strict regex-based lexer with key whitelisting — \fBsource\fR is never used, preventing arbitrary code execution from modified config files. Config file ownership and permissions (\fB600\fR) are verified and enforced on every load.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QEMATE_VM_DIR
Overrides the default VM storage directory (\fB~/QVMs\fR).
.TP
.B LOG_LEVEL
Sets logging verbosity (\fBDEBUG\fR, \fBINFO\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBERROR\fR; default: INFO).
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used by the \fBconfigure\fR command (default: \fBnano\fR).

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/QVMs/VM_NAME/config
Hardened VM configuration file (permissions: 600).
.TP
.I ~/QVMs/VM_NAME/disk.qcow2
Primary QCOW2 disk image. Absent when \fB--disk-dev\fR is used.
.TP
.I ~/QVMs/VM_NAME/logs/qemate.log
General execution log.
.TP
.I ~/QVMs/VM_NAME/logs/error.log
Symlink to the latest timestamped QEMU stderr log.
.TP
.I ~/QVMs/VM_NAME/logs/qemu-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.log
Timestamped stderr output from one QEMU run.
.TP
.I ~/QVMs/VM_NAME/logs/virtiofsd_TAG.log
Per-share virtiofsd daemon log (one per shared folder when using the virtiofs backend).

.SH EXAMPLES
Create and start a Windows 11 VM with TPM and VirtIO drivers:
.EX
qemate create win11 --os-type windows --enable-tpm
qemate start win11 --iso win11.iso --virtio-iso virtio-win.iso
.EE

Create a VM using a physical disk:
.EX
qemate create rawvm --os-type linux --disk-dev /dev/sdb
.EE

Configure a VM (opens $EDITOR):
.EX
qemate configure myvm
.EE

Switch to passt networking (edit NETWORK_TYPE in the config):
.EX
qemate configure myvm
.EE

Add a high-performance shared folder:
.EX
qemate share-add myvm /home/user/work
.EE

Forward a web port:
.EX
qemate port-add myvm 8080:80:tcp
.EE

Resize a stopped VM disk:
.EX
qemate stop myvm
qemate resize myvm +20G
.EE

